USER VISIBLE CHANGES BETWEEN TAO-4.0.8 and TAO-4.0.9
====================================================

. Generated union discriminator setters now throw CORBA::BAD_PARAM when a new
  discriminator would select a different union member. Discriminator values
  selecting the currently active member remain accepted.

USER VISIBLE CHANGES BETWEEN TAO-4.0.7 and TAO-4.0.8
====================================================

. tao_idl now value-initializes generated IDL structure, exception, valuetype,
  valuebox, and union members to prevent fundamental types from having
  indeterminate values after default construction. Generated unions initialize
  their active member and use placement construction where required for
  non-trivial structure members.

. Reworked -ORBTransportIdleTimeout to use a periodic transport-cache scanner
  with monotonic activity timestamps and the new -ORBTransportIdleScanInterval
  option. Active synchronous requests are protected from idle purging.

